          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The expression conventionally and directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Its hesitant, formulaic delivery may bear on sincerity or conviction, but does not remove its clear avowal force; Pierre's immediately preceding thought also represents him as believing that he loves her.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"да и я люблю ее\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"The words themselves do not promise marriage or undertake any future conduct. Pierre and Hélène have already been publicly treated as engaged before he says them, so the surrounding engagement cannot simply be transferred onto this love avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.97,\"reason\":\"The utterance is not represented as a reflexive or uncontrolled discharge of affect. Pierre deliberately recalls what convention requires him to say, and the words sound inadequate to him rather than bursting out spontaneously.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"No core force beyond the truth-conditional love avowal is required. The expression's awkward fulfilment of a social script affects its presentation but does not constitute a distinct residual mode.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Pierre says this privately to Hélène immediately after their families have already celebrated them as an engaged couple. Following her kiss, he remembers the conventional words expected on such an occasion and delivers the avowal awkwardly and with embarrassment.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The target contains no distinct undertaking by Pierre. The engagement has already been socially announced, Hélène has kissed him, and the passage later reports their marriage, but these surrounding events do not turn “Je vous aime” itself into a marriage promise. No explicit response to or acceptance of this particular avowal is reported after it is spoken.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"I recognise the supplied passage as Pierre and Hélène's engagement scene in Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace; the classification relies only on the supplied text.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly supports the avowal's linguistic force and provides some evidence of attraction and self-ascribed love, but Pierre's formulaic delivery, social pressure, fear, and uncertainty prevent a definitive judgment about the depth or sincerity of his affection. Hélène's specific uptake of the spoken avowal is not given.\"}"
